  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ReadICCProfile",
    "file": "imagemagick/coders/jpeg.c",
    "description": "Heap use-after-free caused by stale pointer in error_manager->profile. In ReadICCProfile(), on short-read/error path (i != length), profile is freed via DestroyStringInfo(profile) but error_manager->profile is not cleared before returning FALSE. Later, JPEG error unwinding in ReadJPEGImage_() setjmp handler unconditionally checks error_manager.profile and calls DestroyStringInfo(error_manager.profile), causing a second destroy of already-freed StringInfo and UAF in DestroyStringInfo().",
    "conditions": "Input must reach JPEG ICC marker parsing and trigger ReadICCProfile() allocation, then hit the insufficient-data path (truncated ICC payload / EOF while reading marker body). Data flow here is encoder_jnx_fuzzer -> JNX decode -> embedded JPEG decode; crafted APP2 ICC_PROFILE marker with declared length larger than available bytes causes ReadICCProfile() to free profile and return FALSE while leaving error_manager->profile dangling, then ReadJPEGImage_ cleanup dereferences/frees it again."
  },
